# vew_image data source

Reads an existing image by exact ID. Terminal image states stay visible. A
missing image is an error.

Permission: project assignment and `clients/packaging/pipeline.read`.

## Selectors

| Attribute | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `project_id` | string | Required VEW project identifier. |
| `image_id` | string | Required exact image identifier. |

## Computed attributes

`pipeline_id`, `status`, and nullable `image_upstream_id`. A null upstream ID
stays null; it is not replaced with an empty string.

```hcl
data "vew_image" "existing" {
  project_id = var.project_id
  image_id   = var.image_id
}

output "upstream_image_id" {
  value = data.vew_image.existing.image_upstream_id
}
```

This data source cannot consume `vew_image_build` progress as a structured
value during the same action invocation. Use an explicit known ID or
`vew_images` on a later refresh.

